 "method": "STFT (1024-pt Hann, 128 hop) dominant-peak pitch track in 1.3-9.5 kHz; note segmentation on the 1.5-9 kHz band Hilbert envelope (3 ms smoothing): body pass onset -26 dB / offset -33 dB rel. file peak (min off-time 15 ms, min note 30 ms), plus a sensitive pass (onset -38 / offset -45 dB, min off 20 ms, min note 40 ms) whose additions were kept only with median pitch prominence >= 8 dB. Note f_start/f_end = median track over first/last 20%; f_med = whole-note median; f_peak/f_min = 95th/5th percentile. harm2/harm3 = median ratio of STFT magnitude at 2x/3x the tracked peak to the peak itself; subharm = same at f/2. peak_amp_rel = max of the band envelope (linear, signal peak-normalized) within the note. Templates = per-note tracks resampled to 16 normalized points, median across instances. Songs = note groups split at gaps > 1.2 s. Song base frequency = median f_med of the song's sustained notes (dur >= 0.25 s). Type rules (this bird, by duration/contour): W = song-initial note, dur >= 0.15 s, |f_end-f_start|/f_start < 3% (flat lead whistle); sustained notes (dur >= 0.15 s): rise >= 10% -> U, fall >= 15% -> D, else S; short notes (dur < 0.15 s): dur < 0.07 s -> C, rise >= 8% -> u, fall >= 8% -> d, else C. The one sensitive-pass fragment at 0.16 s (unreliable contour, amp 0.014) is typed x and NOT templated. Tremolo: per sustained note, FFT of the 1.5-9 kHz band envelope (1 ms smoothing) \u2014 peak rate in 8-60 Hz and a percentile depth index. Contamination scan: short-time RMS in 0.25 s windows for the 60-500 Hz band and full band; a swell = 1 s-smoothed level > file median + 7 dB sustained >= 1.5 s (spans < 2 s apart merged). Gap contrast: 0.25 s full-band RMS windows, p10 (gap floor) vs p90 (phrase). Grid values (durations, transition periods, song pause) are design choices for the electronic end of the morph: nearest 32nd-note multiple at 112 BPM (0.067 s) with floors of 1 step (durations) / 2 steps (periods); song pause to the nearest beat.",
